<article class="env-lemma" id="05J7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05J7">Lemma <span data-tag="05J7">38.16.4</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes which is of finite type. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a finite type quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $s \in S$. Let $(S', s') \to (S, s)$ be a morphism of pointed schemes. If $S' \to S$ is quasi-finite at $s'$ and $\mathcal{F}$ is pure along $X_ s$, then $\mathcal{F}_{S'}$ is pure along $X_{s'}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It $(T \to S', t' \leadsto t, \xi )$ is an impurity of $\mathcal{F}_{S'}$ above $s'$ with $T \to S'$ quasi-finite at $t$, then $(T \to S, t' \to t, \xi )$ is an impurity of $\mathcal{F}$ above $s$ with $T \to S$ quasi-finite at $t$, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01TL" data-tag="01TL">29.21.12</a>. Hence the lemma follows immediately from the characterization (2) of purity given following Definition <a href="/tag/05J4" data-tag="05J4">38.16.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>